      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Worked Example",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Release 2.4 gets 14 cherry-picks from main. What breaks in month three?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Same code, ==different SHAs== — Git sees no relationship",
            "`git merge main` re-offers all 14 patches",
            "Patch-id drops only __byte-identical__ ones; conflict-resolved picks stay",
            "Every release repeats it: **duplication debt** compounds"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "git log --oneline main..rel-2.4",
            "# 14 picks, none recorded as merged",
            "git cherry -v main rel-2.4",
            "# '+' = still unmerged upstream"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Find What To Pick",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git cherry -v main topic",
            "# '+' = unmerged, '-' = already in",
            "git log --oneline --no-merges \\",
            "  main..topic"
          ],
          "note": "`git cherry` matches by patch-id"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Bisect Session",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Command",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`bisect start`",
              "open session"
            ],
            [
              "`bad` / `good <sha>`",
              "set the bounds"
            ],
            [
              "`skip`",
              "untestable commit"
            ],
            [
              "`log > b.log` / `replay b.log`",
              "save / redo run"
            ],
            [
              "`reset`",
              "back to your branch"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git bisect start HEAD v1.9 &&",
            "git bisect run ./check.sh",
            "# 0=good 1=bad 125=skip",
            "git bisect visualize   # see range"
          ],
          "note": "`--term-old`/`--term-new` rename good/bad"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Reflog Selectors",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Selector",
            "Points at"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`HEAD@{1}`",
              "one move ago"
            ],
            [
              "`main@{1}`",
              "main before last update"
            ],
            [
              "`HEAD@{2.days.ago}`",
              "by wall-clock time"
            ],
            [
              "`HEAD~2`",
              "**two commits back** (DAG)"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 3,
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Undo and Rescue",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git reset --hard HEAD@{1}",
            "git reset --hard ORIG_HEAD",
            "git branch rescue <sha>",
            "git fsck --full --unreachable",
            "git show <dangling-sha>"
          ],
          "note": "ORIG_HEAD = pre reset/merge/rebase"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Search Instead of Bisect",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`git log -S'apiKey'` — ==pickaxe==, when a string appeared or died",
            "`git log -L :parseUrl:src/api.ts` — one function's whole life",
            "`git log --oneline -- path/` — commits touching one path"
          ],
          "ink": "blue"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "git",
      "subtitle": "All three tools, one page"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Safety, Destructive Commands & Mistakes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Safety and Config",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git push --force-with-lease",
            "git branch backup-$(date +%s)",
            "git config gc.reflogExpire 90.days",
            "git config core.logAllRefUpdates true"
          ],
          "note": "never `gc --prune=now` mid-investigation"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`gc.reflogExpireUnreachable=30.days` — orphans die sooner",
            "`core.logAllRefUpdates` off = ==no reflog exists at all==",
            "Bare repos default it to **false** — no undo journal there"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. The Destructive Triad",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Command",
            "Destroys",
            "Recoverable?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`reset --hard`",
              "tree + index + HEAD",
              "**commits** yes via reflog — uncommitted tree/index ==no=="
            ],
            [
              "`checkout -- .`",
              "working tree only",
              "==no=="
            ],
            [
              "`clean -fd`",
              "untracked files",
              "==no=="
            ],
            [
              "`gc --prune=now`",
              "unreachable objects",
              "only from backup"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 0,
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "9. Mistakes That Bite",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Pick without `-x` — no trail back to the __upstream fix__",
            "Forget `A^..B` — commit **A** silently dropped from the range",
            "Bisect a flaky test — a ==confidently wrong== first bad commit",
            "Assume the reflog in CI — a fresh clone has **one line**"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "ink": "red"
        },
