  "caption": {
    "text": "Part 2 of GIT TIME TRAVEL. Git never really deletes your work — you just lose the pointer to it. This carousel is a field guide to the three tools that get it back: cherry-pick to replay a commit on another branch, bisect to binary-search history for the commit that broke things, and reflog as the local undo journal that remembers every HEAD you've moved. Object model underneath, real command sequences, and the mistakes that bite people.",
